    "author_ids": [],
    "abstract": "In a subset of repeat expansion disorders, nuclear dysfunction extends beyond the originating locus through poorly understood mechanisms. Studies from the C9orf72 gene indicate that repeat RNAs interact with the genome in trans, suggesting that disease-specific repeat RNA sequences and structures may similarly contribute to pathogenic mechanisms in some of these disorders.",
